{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "toolName": "dyad_analysis",
  "serverName": "Analysis",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "stability": "stable",
  "methodId": "MotifFinder.AnalyzeDyads",
  "docRef": "Seqeron.Genomics.Analysis/MotifFinder.DyadAnalysis.cs#L56",
  "description": "RSAT `dyad-analysis` (van Helden, Rios & Collado-Vides 2000, NAR 28:1808): over-represented spaced dyads M1 n{s} M2 — two monads of length m separated by s unspecified residues, s in [minSpacing, maxSpacing] — of type any / dr (M2 = M1) / ir (M2 = rc M1) / rep. Per spacing T_s = Σ max(0, L − 2m − s + 1) positions; `countOverlapping` = false (RSAT default `-noov`) discards an occurrence starting < 2m + s after the last counted one of the same dyad (or of its reverse complement with both strands). Both strands (default `-2str`): D and D' = rc(M2) n{s} rc(M1) form one pattern, occ summed. exp_freq from the input monad frequencies f(M) (single strand): f(M1)·f(M2) (+ f(rc M1)·f(rc M2) with both strands unless D is a reverse palindrome), or from a monad / dyad frequency table; exp_occ = exp_freq · occ_sum_s; z = (occ − exp_occ)/√(T_s·p·(2·ovlp − 1 − (4m+1)·p)); occ_P = P(X ≥ occ), X ~ Bin(T_s, exp_freq); occ_E = occ_P × tested dyads; occ_sig = −log10 occ_E. `minCount` <= 0 tests every combination of observed monads (RSAT without `-lth occ`). Equals RSAT dyad-analysis 1.78 (single strand ≤ 1.3e-14 on 200 runs / 14,746 dyads); deliberate differences (RSAT code defects, documented in the algorithm doc): with both strands RSAT drops pairs seen only as their lexicographically larger member, `rep` counts palindromic monads twice, and with `-return zscore` RSAT drops dyads whose variance is ≤ 0; z-scores are not rounded to 2 decimals.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "sequences": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "description": "DNA sequences"
      },
      "monadLength": {
        "type": "integer",
        "minimum": 1,
        "default": 3,
        "description": "Monad length m (RSAT -l, >= 1, default 3)"
      },
      "minSpacing": {
        "type": "integer",
        "minimum": 0,
        "default": 0,
        "description": "Minimal spacing (>= 0, default 0)"
      },
      "maxSpacing": {
        "type": "integer",
        "minimum": 0,
        "default": 20,
        "description": "Maximal spacing (>= minSpacing, default 20)"
      },
      "dyadType": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "any",
          "dr",
          "ir",
          "rep"
        ],
        "default": "any",
        "description": "'any' (default), 'dr', 'ir' or 'rep'"
      },
      "strands": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "both",
          "single"
        ],
        "default": "both",
        "description": "'both' (-2str, default) or 'single' (-1str)"
      },
      "countOverlapping": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": false,
        "description": "Count overlapping occurrences (-ovlp); default false = RSAT -noov"
      },
      "minCount": {
        "type": "integer",
        "default": 1,
        "description": "Occurrence threshold (RSAT -lth occ, default 1); <= 0 tests every monad combination"
      },
      "background": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "monads",
          "monad_table",
          "dyad_table"
        ],
        "default": "monads",
        "description": "'monads' (default), 'monad_table' (needs monadFrequencies) or 'dyad_table' (needs dyadFrequencies)"
      },
      "monadFrequencies": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "description": "Monad -> expected frequency (background 'monad_table', RSAT -mncf)"
      },
      "dyadFrequencies": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "description": "Dyad in RSAT notation (e.g. 'acgn{4}tta') -> expected single-strand frequency (background 'dyad_table', RSAT -expfreq)"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "sequences"
    ]
  },
